---
import { OPEN_PARTICIPATION } from '../../lib/config';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/paths';
---

<Base title="Discussion rules" description="How discussions are chosen and moderated.">
  <h1>Discussion rules</h1>

  <h2>How a discussion works</h2>
  <p>
    Each discussion asks one neutral question. You vote agree, disagree or pass on short statements, and you can add a
    statement of your own. Pol.is groups people by how they vote, so the results show both where opinion divides and
    what most people agree on.
  </p>

  <h2>What a statement must be</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>One idea, in a sentence or two, that others can agree or disagree with.</li>
    <li>About the question, not about another participant.</li>
    <li>
      Free of personal attacks, slurs, threats, private information about anyone, advertising and links to campaigns.
    </li>
    <li>Not a duplicate of a statement that is already there.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Moderators approve statements before others see them. We reject statements that break these rules, whatever view
    they express. We never edit a statement. Rejection decisions do not depend on politics or party.
  </p>

  <h2>Who chooses topics</h2>
  <p>
    The site’s maintainers open discussions. Anyone can ask for a discussion on a council matter, bill, executive order
    or Supreme Court decision; the number of requests is shown publicly and helps us choose. We do not open discussions
    on candidates or elections.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can take part</h2>
  {OPEN_PARTICIPATION ? (
    <p>
      Anyone can read, vote and write; you don’t need an account. Some discussions are meant for residents of a state,
      the city or a council district, and we ask you to take part only where you live. This is an honor system, not
      identity verification, so results describe the people who took part, not a scientific sample.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      Anyone can read. To vote or write you must be signed in, and some discussions are limited to residents of a state,
      the city or a council district, based on the address you saved. This is an honor system, not identity
      verification, so results describe the people who took part, not a scientific sample.
    </p>
  )}

  <p class="small">
    <a href={href('privacy/')}>Privacy</a> · <a href={href('discussions/')}>All discussions</a>
  </p>
</Base>
